-- title:
--   Two-component exhaustion at level Nℓ: product of values is a non-unit
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime such that the valuation of the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $v_A(\ell) < 1$ and $\ell \nmid N$. Let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of the field $F_0 = \mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}(N\ell)) \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ satisfying `IsAtkinLehnerAutFull N ℓ σ`, i.e. for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $N$ the automorphism $\sigma$ interchanges the $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$ and $j(q^{d\ell})$. Let $W$ be a place of the base-changed field $L = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, F_0)$, that is, a proper valuation subring of $L$ containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring; $W.\mathrm{ord}$ denotes $-\log$ of the associated adic valuation. Assume there is $c \in A$ with $W.\mathrm{ord}(\bar{j} - c) > 0$, where $\bar{j}$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$ in $L$. Let $e, f \in L$ each be a root of a monic polynomial over the subring $\mathrm{affineBaseFin}(N\ell, A)$ generated by the constants from $A$ together with $\bar{j}$, and let $a, b \in A$ satisfy $W.\mathrm{ord}(e - a) > 0$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(f - b) > 0$. Assume every Laurent coefficient of $e$ has $A$-valuation $< 1$, and every Laurent coefficient of the image of $f$ under the automorphism of $L$ induced from $\sigma$ by base change has $A$-valuation $< 1$. Then $v_A(ab) < 1$.
--
--   This is the Fourier-expansion form of the exhaustion of the special fibre at $\ell$ of the level-$N\ell$ modular curve by its two components, the two cusp charts being matched by the Atkin–Lehner involution: a point cannot reduce to an interior point of both components simultaneously, so the matched values $a$ and $b$ cannot both be units. It is used in the identification of the places of the fibre model attached to the cusp charts, in [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d1_of_cuspChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d1_of_cuspChart) and its level-wise variant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_twoComponentExhaustion_valuation_mul_lt_one_of_ord_sub_pos.lean

